<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n69967" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νεάπολις</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾱ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>new city,</i> pr. n. of several cities,
				<u>Neapolis</u>: at first in two words, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νέα πόλις,</span> gen. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νέης πόλιος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.91
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.50
			</span></i>; later in one, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νεάπολις,</span>
			gen. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νεαπόλεως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					2.5.40
				</span></i>
			, dat. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νεαπόλει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					1.2.13
				</span></i>
			: hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νεοπολίτης</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῑ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.191.31
			</span></i>, al., later <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νεᾱπολίτης</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Tab.Heracl.</u>
				1.187
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				736
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				1.20.14
			</span></i>, etc., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				9.26
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
